  "articleBody": "Deciding between a surface refresh and a complete kitchen renovation comes down to layout limits, plumbing conditions, and long-term household goals.\n\nKey Differences\nA cosmetic refresh preserves your current footprint while replacing cabinet fronts, repainting drywall, upgrading counters, or installing modern tile backsplashes. A full remodel strips the room to the wall framing to reconfigure working zones, move sinks, reroute electrical boxes, and upgrade structural supports.\n\nWhen to Choose Each\nChoose a refresh if your current workflow functions well, your cabinet boxes remain structurally sturdy, and your plumbing and wiring meet modern safety codes. Opt for a full remodel if you want to remove an adjoining dining wall, widen tight cooking aisles, or address recurring water damage underneath worn flooring.\n\nCost and Timeline Tradeoffs\nA cosmetic update takes significantly less time and requires minimal permitting review. A complete renovation takes longer because it involves plan reviews, multi-trade coordination, and scheduled municipal inspections.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\nIf your project touches gas supply pipes, structural framing, or code-mandated electrical circuits, hire a general contractor. Call HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to discuss which scope matches your Aurora or Denver home.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
